WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.307
Hello, and welcome to week four: scale a known fact.

2
00:00:05.307 --> 00:00:12.807
By the end, you will be able to use a times-table fact to multiply and divide with tens and hundreds.

3
00:00:12.807 --> 00:00:14.742
Let's start.

4
00:00:15.892 --> 00:00:18.342
Four groups of three make twelve.

5
00:00:18.342 --> 00:00:23.087
Say the fact: four times three equals twelve.

6
00:00:24.987 --> 00:00:27.588
Now every counter is worth ten.

7
00:00:27.588 --> 00:00:29.689
Count the tens in the four groups.

8
00:00:29.689 --> 00:00:32.442
Pause the video and have a go.

9
00:00:41.092 --> 00:00:43.333
Each group is three tens.

10
00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:50.020
Four groups of three tens make twelve tens, and twelve tens is one hundred and twenty.

11
00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:57.474
Thirty is ten times the size of three, so the answer is ten times the size of twelve:

12
00:00:57.474 --> 00:01:01.336
write the fact you know, and the new fact under it.

13
00:01:03.236 --> 00:01:04.641
Keep the same groups.

14
00:01:04.641 --> 00:01:10.253
How many groups of three tens make twelve tens?

15
00:01:10.253 --> 00:01:12.345
Pause the video and have a go.

16
00:01:20.995 --> 00:01:22.969
Count the groups: four.

17
00:01:22.969 --> 00:01:27.392
So one hundred and twenty divided by thirty equals four.

18
00:01:27.392 --> 00:01:32.129
The answer is how many groups, so it is four, not forty:

19
00:01:32.129 --> 00:01:38.220
one hundred and twenty and thirty are both ten times the size of twelve and three.

20
00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:43.359
Now every counter is worth one hundred.

21
00:01:43.359 --> 00:01:45.344
Count the hundreds.

22
00:01:45.344 --> 00:01:48.365
Pause the video and have a go.

23
00:01:57.015 --> 00:02:03.551
Four groups of three hundreds make twelve hundreds, which is one thousand two hundred.

24
00:02:03.551 --> 00:02:08.950
The same fact with a bigger unit: three hundred is a hundred times the size of three,

25
00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:12.847
so the answer is a hundred times the size of twelve.

26
00:02:14.747 --> 00:02:19.577
Put the twelve hundreds together, then share them into four equal groups.

27
00:02:19.577 --> 00:02:23.039
Pause the video and have a go.

28
00:02:31.689 --> 00:02:37.030
Twelve hundreds shared into four groups is three hundreds in each group,

29
00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:41.105
because twelve divided by four equals three.

30
00:02:41.105 --> 00:02:47.939
So one thousand two hundred divided by four equals three hundred.

31
00:02:49.839 --> 00:02:54.030
Dividing by three shares the twelve tens into three groups:

32
00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:57.502
four tens in each group, which is forty.

33
00:02:57.502 --> 00:03:03.353
Dividing by thirty asks how many groups of three tens there are: four groups.

34
00:03:03.353 --> 00:03:07.575
Say the unit, and you will know which answer is which.

35
00:03:09.475 --> 00:03:11.704
Here is a worked example.

36
00:03:11.704 --> 00:03:21.546
Use three times nine equals twenty-seven to work out three times ninety and three times nine hundred.

37
00:03:22.796 --> 00:03:28.996
Three groups of nine tens are twenty-seven tens, which is two hundred and seventy.

38
00:03:28.996 --> 00:03:32.908
Three groups of nine hundreds are twenty-seven hundreds,

39
00:03:32.908 --> 00:03:35.579
which is two thousand seven hundred.

40
00:03:35.579 --> 00:03:37.471
Pause the video.

41
00:03:37.471 --> 00:03:40.375
Try the next one in your booklet.

42
00:03:49.675 --> 00:03:51.556
Now let's try a question together.

43
00:03:51.556 --> 00:04:02.400
Use three times five equals fifteen to work out one thousand five hundred divided by three and one hundred and fifty divided by fifty.

44
00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:05.443
Pause the video and have a go.

45
00:04:14.093 --> 00:04:19.526
Fifteen hundreds shared into three groups is five hundreds each: five hundred.

46
00:04:19.526 --> 00:04:24.472
Fifteen tens in groups of five tens make three groups: three.

47
00:04:24.472 --> 00:04:26.953
Well done if you got it.

48
00:04:28.853 --> 00:04:30.699
Now try it in your booklet.

49
00:04:30.699 --> 00:04:34.971
Remember: name the unit and use the fact you know:

50
00:04:34.971 --> 00:04:38.373
four groups of three tens are twelve tens,

51
00:04:38.373 --> 00:04:44.863
which is one hundred and twenty, and twelve tens in groups of three tens make four groups.

52
00:04:44.863 --> 00:04:46.311
Good luck.
